<article class="env-lemma" id="00O1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00O1">Lemma <span data-tag="00O1">10.78.6</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a flat local homomorphism of local rings. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module. Then $M$ is finite projective over $R$ if and only if $M \otimes _ R S$ is finite projective over $S$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/00NX" data-tag="00NX">10.78.2</a> being finite projective over a local ring is the same thing as being finite free. Suppose that $M \otimes _ R S$ is a finite free $S$-module. Pick $x_1, \ldots , x_ r \in M$ whose images in $M/\mathfrak m_ RM$ form a basis over $\kappa (\mathfrak m)$. Then we see that $x_1 \otimes 1, \ldots , x_ r \otimes 1$ are a basis for $M \otimes _ R S$. This implies that the map $R^{\oplus r} \to M, (a_ i) \mapsto \sum a_ i x_ i$ becomes an isomorphism after tensoring with $S$. By faithful flatness of $R \to S$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/00HR" data-tag="00HR">10.39.17</a> we see that it is an isomorphism. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>